WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.160 --> 00:00:05.759
Cerium is one of only two elements which,
if you strike it, will make

00:00:05.759 --> 00:00:12.860
sparks. One of them is iron and the other
one is cerium. And so I bought

00:00:12.860 --> 00:00:16.210
this when I was on holiday a year ago. I haven’t
had the chance to use

00:00:16.210 --> 00:00:22.180
it. It contains, it consists of a rod here
which claims to have several

00:00:22.180 --> 00:00:29.250
metals including cerium. Let’s see if it
sparks.

00:00:29.250 --> 00:00:36.879
Ok so cerium, element number 58, has some
bizarre uses, would you

00:00:36.879 --> 00:00:38.980
believe it’s used in self-cleaning ovens.

00:00:38.980 --> 00:00:48.649
So it’s not very easy to do but, once you
get the hang of it, it does go

00:00:48.649 --> 00:00:50.079
quite well.

00:00:50.079 --> 00:00:55.219
Cerium also has uses such for staining glass.
So if you want to stain your

00:00:55.219 --> 00:01:01.960
glass yellow then you could use cerium in
that.

00:01:01.960 --> 00:01:07.760
What is happening is that tiny pieces of cerium
are being knocked off

00:01:07.760 --> 00:01:12.330
and, in the air, they just burst into flames.
So, I think, the property is,

00:01:12.330 --> 00:01:17.090
not so much that it forms a spark, but that
you can knock off the right

00:01:17.090 --> 00:01:21.820
size lumps to make them burn. These things
that are being knocked off

00:01:21.820 --> 00:01:28.170
are probably just a few nanometres, that’s
a thousandth-millionth of a

00:01:28.170 --> 00:01:34.000
metre across so they’re very tiny size.
So then the surface area is high

00:01:34.000 --> 00:01:38.210
because it’s small so it has a large surface
compared to its volume. And

00:01:38.210 --> 00:01:44.080
so it reacts with oxygen very rapidly and
heats up and bursts into flame.

00:01:44.080 --> 00:01:51.430
The point about cerium is that very small
particles of cerium oxide are

00:01:51.430 --> 00:01:58.630
now becoming quite important in various areas
of technology. There’s a

00:01:58.630 --> 00:02:03.290
company, or several companies, that are using
nano particles of cerium

00:02:03.290 --> 00:02:08.690
oxide as an additive for fuels to make a particular
diesel fuel to try and

00:02:08.690 --> 00:02:11.900
make it burn better and give more power when
you are driving diesel

00:02:11.900 --> 00:02:19.320
cars. And here in Nottingham we are trying
to develop new ways of

00:02:19.320 --> 00:02:23.800
making these nano particles by reacting cerium
with high temperature

00:02:23.800 --> 00:02:26.390
water and it’s been quite successful.

00:02:26.390 --> 00:02:30.570
It’s also used in organic synthesis by chemists
for making organic

00:02:30.570 --> 00:02:33.880
molecules because it can be very reactive
under certain circumstances.

00:02:33.880 --> 00:02:39.390
Cerium is also used in permanent magnets for
obvious applications in

00:02:39.390 --> 00:02:40.310
magnetism.

